{
  "_comment": [
    "Roadmap §71 (client configuration) and §73 (new client provisioning).",
    "",
    "Copy this to client.json, fill it in, and scripts/setup.sh applies it —",
    "that is the 'set client configuration' step in §73's flow, which until now",
    "was a checklist rather than a command. You can also apply it any time with:",
    "",
    "    docker compose run --rm wpcli wp algerian-commerce settings --from=client.json",
    "",
    "This file holds NO SECRETS. API keys, tokens and webhook secrets live in",
    ".env and nowhere else (docs/SECURITY.md) — an options row is readable by any",
    "plugin and survives in every database dump. client.json is safe to commit",
    "for a real client; .env never is.",
    "",
    "Three things are deliberately NOT here, and the API refuses them by name",
    "with the reason attached:",
    "",
    "  currency   WooCommerce owns it and records it per order, so changing it",
    "             later splits the order book instead of converting it.",
    "             setup.sh sets it once, at provisioning.",
    "  features   ENABLE_COD, ENABLE_CHARGILY, ... are environment variables read",
    "             once at bootstrap to decide which providers register. Set them",
    "             in .env and restart. GET /settings reports them.",
    "  providers  Read-only. It reports which providers actually registered,",
    "             which follows from their flags AND their credentials — a flag",
    "             that is on with no key produces a provider that never loads.",
    "",
    "Every field below is optional. Delete what does not apply."
  ],

